# Git⟦f:bridges⟧ and forge⟦/f⟧

⟦f:git-tracking⟧- **Repository**: A git repository, identified by its **repository identity**, a
  bound root commit, the same on every node with a git clone, shallow clones
  included, else a provisional node-local identity bound later (LANE-02). The
  first bind is a structural event ParleyInn records at the first hook event;
  binding by hand or rebinding is a widening principal act. It has remotes⟦f:work-rooms⟧ and
  may carry room trailers⟦f:export-bundles⟧, bundles as git refs⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-carrier⟧ and the git carrier's segments⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:git-tracking⟧- **Branch**: A git branch, identified by repository identity, remote URL and
  branch name. A branch with no remote has a provisional node-local identity,
  rebound when it is pushed.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:git-tracking⟧- **Commit**: A git commit.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:git-tracking⟧- **Worktree**: A git working tree on a node, where a run edits a branch; its
  repository's **git directory** is git's own store of objects and refs. Paths
  from hook input may name a run's worktree or its git directory only for
  reading (SEC-18).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:bridges⟧- **Forge**: The service that keeps remotes, pull requests, reviews and ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branch⟦/f⟧
  protection. It approves and lands; ParleyInn does neither, and its **forge
  reports** count as `asserted` (LANE-08).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:bridges⟧- **Pull request**: The forge's review object for a ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branch⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Check**: A command executed, or expected to execute, on a tree, with its
  exit status once it ends; its **check state** is one of §9.7.2's. A check is
  expected when one of the ⟦f:intent-criteria⟧intent's criteria⟦/f⟧ names its command (LANE-20)⟦f:bridges⟧; a
  check the forge reports, one of its **required checks** included, is a forge
  report, `asserted`, not a result⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Result**: What a room's seats established: a check passing or failing on a
  **tree** (git's snapshot of a ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit's⟦/f⟧ files), or a claim stated in text. It
  names the ⟦f:intent-criteria⟧intent⟦/f⟧ version and carries one evidence class; it is derived from
  the events it rests on and addressed by the event recording its exit status or
  its claim's text.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Evidence**: The checks⟦f:ci-attestation⟧, CI attestations⟦/f⟧ or text a result rests on.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Evidence class**: Of a result, ranked: `claim` (text, or tool output alone)
  < `own check`⟦f:witness-check⟧ < `witness check`⟦/f⟧⟦f:ci-attestation⟧ < `CI attested`⟦/f⟧ (LANE-05).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Own check**: A check the hook handlers recorded on the node of the run that
  made the edits, run on the latest ⟦f:git-tracking⟧worktree checkpoint⟦/f⟧ plus the recorded edits;
  otherwise its result is marked `unbound` and counts as a `claim`.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:witness-check⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Witness check**: A check re-run⟦f:launcher⟧ through the launcher⟦/f⟧ on a fresh checkout of
  the exact ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit⟦/f⟧, with network denied and no write access outside that checkout, the
  home and the harness configuration included, by a node whose **git identity** (the
  author and commit-signing identities its git configuration sets) authored no
  ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit on the branch⟦/f⟧ since it left its base⟦f:git-tracking⟧ (a **commit author** is git's
  author of a commit, never a seat)⟦/f⟧. Where the platform cannot deny network or
  such writes, ParleyInn refuses the witness check (OWN-18).⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
⟦f:ci-attestation⟧- **CI attestation**: A ⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧check's⟦/f⟧ exit status for the exact ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit⟦/f⟧, signed by a CI
  key the room's owner enrolled, recorded in the room so every principal sees
  the same class (LANE-22); a ⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧result⟦/f⟧ resting on one is `CI attested`.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:work-rooms⟧- **Landing**: Git⟦f:bridges⟧ or the forge⟦/f⟧ merging ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commits⟦/f⟧ into the ⟦f:git-tracking⟧repository's default
  branch⟦/f⟧⟦f:bridges⟧ or a ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branch⟦/f⟧ the forge protects⟦/f⟧. ParleyInn never lands anything⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧, and a
  landing is never a verdict⟦/f⟧. A ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branch⟦/f⟧ lands when its head lands.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:work-rooms⟧- **Landing link**: The qualified link from a landed ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit⟦/f⟧ to a room, carrying
  a proof class, derived by ParleyInn from the record alone: the clone facts it
  reads (landed ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commits⟦/f⟧, patch ids, trees) are recorded as structural events.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:work-rooms⟧- **Proof class**: Of a landing link. Proven: `same ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit⟦/f⟧`, `same patch`, `same
  tree`. Not proven: `likely`, `asserted`, and `not proven` with a reason
  (LANE-06). `asserted` is also the mark on⟦f:bridges⟧ forge reports and⟦/f⟧ room trailers.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:work-rooms⟧- **Room trailer**: The `ParleyInn-Room:` line in a ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit⟦/f⟧ message, naming a room;
  ParleyInn adds one to every ⟦f:git-tracking⟧commit on a room's branch⟦/f⟧ (LANE-28). Each
  `ParleyInn-Link:` line is a trailer link. It counts as `asserted` until proven
  (LANE-28).⟦/f⟧
- **Qualified links**: Every link is named by what it connects: ⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧a branch link
  (room to branch), ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:bridges⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧a pull-request link (branch to its pull request, derived by
  ParleyInn from forge bridge events), ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧⟦f:intent-criteria⟧a criterion link (result to criterion), ⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧a
  range link (⟦f:conversation⟧post or ⟦/f⟧pin to an address range), a parent link (subagent run to
  parent run)⟦f:delegation-grants⟧, a delegation link (delegating run to the delegate's run, under a
  delegation grant)⟦/f⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧⟦f:principal-keys⟧⟦f:access-tokens⟧, an invite link (which connects nothing: it carries an
  access token)⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧, a landing link and a trailer link (commit to a pin⟦f:conversation⟧, post or
  marked range⟦/f⟧)⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧. "Link" never stands alone, except as the name of the room act
  that adds one range link⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧, branch link⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧⟦f:intent-criteria⟧ or criterion link⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧.
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Comparison**: A side-by-side view of two ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branches⟦/f⟧: each one's exposure,
  results and evidence. It picks no winner.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Outcome**: What a room's runs have produced so far: the heads of the
  ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branches⟦/f⟧ it names, their results and evidence, as verdicts assess them.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:presentations⟧- **Presentation**: What a seat put in the outcome window, such as a dev
  server's URL (inert text the person opens in their own browser), a build
  artifact, a file or a diff, with the seat and ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branch⟦/f⟧. Every presentation is
  shown as inert data: never executed, nor loaded as a page⟦f:browser-room-view⟧ in the browser room
  view⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Verdict**: A person's `met`, `not met` or `needs changes` on one ⟦f:intent-criteria⟧criterion⟦/f⟧:
  a `verdict` pin, recorded as a neutral principal act (OWN-27) by any person
  whose device seat in the room has the pin capability, bound to the ⟦f:intent-criteria⟧intent
  version⟦/f⟧, the heads of every ⟦f:git-tracking⟧branch⟦/f⟧ the room names, and the results and
  evidence shown. It goes stale when any of them changes. It is never edited: a
  newer verdict of the same person on the same ⟦f:intent-criteria⟧criterion⟦/f⟧ supersedes it, and
  unpinning one is neutral. ParleyInn never derives one⟦f:service-accounts⟧; service accounts contribute
  evidence instead⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
